I found a real bug. Line 1012-1014: operator precedence issue. `|| has lower precedence than &&` in Rust, so this evaluates as:

```
--upload-file || (-t AND (ftp:// || sftp://))
```

This means ANY curl command with --upload-file triggers regardless of protocol (probably the intent), BUT the -t check requires ftp/sftp which is correct. However, there's actually a subtle false-positive risk here: `-t ` is a very short pattern that could match other flags/args. Let me look for more significant issues.

